    "insights": [
      "Lipschitz closed curves generalize smooth closed curves: replace ContDiff ℝ 1 with LipschitzWith K",
      "Key axiom: Wirtinger inequality extends to Lipschitz (absolutely continuous) functions: LipschitzWith K f → ∫f² ≤ ∫(f'²) when f has zero mean",
      "Key axiom: Arc-length reparametrization works for Lipschitz curves via inverse function theorem for monotone AC maps",
      "The proof structure is IDENTICAL to the smooth case (same arithmetic kernel isoperimetric_from_wirtinger_bounds)",
      "Every SmoothClosedCurve is a LipschitzClosedCurve via toLipschitz embedding (circumference and area preserved by definition equality)",
      "Square (piecewise-linear, Lipschitz not smooth): C=4a, A=a², ratio=π/4 < 1 PROVED without sorries",
      "Circumference/area definitions are literally identical for smooth and Lipschitz curves (same integral formula)"
    ],
